.SH NAME
QTextDecoder \- State-based decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
\fC#include <qtextcodec.h>\fR
.PP
.SS "Public Members"
.in +1c
.ti -1c
.BI "virtual \fB~QTextDecoder\fR ()"
.br
.ti -1c
.BI "virtual QString \fBtoUnicode\fR ( const char * " "chars" ", int len )"
.br
.in -1c
.SH DESCRIPTION
State-based decoder
.PP
A QTextEncoder converts a text format into Unicode, remembering any state that is required between calls.
.PP
See also: QTextCodec::makeEncoder().
.SH MEMBER FUNCTION DOCUMENTATION
.SH "QTextDecoder::~QTextDecoder () \fC[virtual]\fR"
Destroys the decoder.
.SH "QString QTextDecoder::toUnicode ( const char * chars, int len ) \fC[virtual]\fR"
Converts the first \fIlen\fR bytes at \fIchars\fR to Unicode, returning the result.
.PP
If not all characters are used (eg. only part of a multi-byte
encoding is at the end of the characters), the decoder remembers
enough state to continue with the next call to this function.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
